# B87 — the exact repro. A free function whose name ends in `!` used to be
# parsed as a MACRO call (`parser/expr/atoms.rs` stripped the `!` and emitted
# `ExprKind::MacroCall`), nothing downstream recognised the name, and MIR's
# macro lowering ended in a `_ => Ok(None)` catch-all that emitted no code at
# all. So `shout!(5)` compiled without a single diagnostic and the call
# vanished: the program printed `before` then `after`.
#
# The pin is the middle line. If the call is ever dropped again the output
# loses `shouting 5` while still "passing" compilation, which is exactly how
# this defect survived.
def shout!(x: Int)
  puts "shouting #{x}"
end

def main
  puts "before"
  shout!(5)
  puts "after"
end
